            <ArticleTitle>TNP-assisted fascial closure in a patient with acute abdomen and abdominal compartment syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>65-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Topical negative pressure was applied to prevent abdominal compartment syndrome in a patient following surgery for an acute abdomen. It delayed fascial closure, protected the underlying bowel and facilitated abdominal re-entry.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
